timebench, the code of TIME (https://github.com/zqiao11/TIME), declares in
the pyproject.toml of commit c633e232fbba20c54242ffcac55e77c50440f470
`license = {text = "MIT"}` and `authors = [{name = "Zhongzheng Qiao"}]`, but
neither its repository at that commit nor its distribution holds a license
file. Its README.md shows a badge whose label reads "License: MIT" and whose
image reads "License: Apache-2.0", linked to the Apache-2.0 text. The text
below is not a file of timebench's: it is the MIT License as the Open Source
Initiative publishes it, in the name of the author pyproject.toml gives, with
no year, since timebench gives none. The copy of
src/timebench/evaluation/data.py keeps that file's own notice as well,
Salesforce's Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-gift-eval).

